  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "24. Core Abilities",
    "ruleNumber": "24.02",
    "summary": "Copies of one core or weapon ability never stack, even if their numbers or keywords differ; the controlling player picks which one applies at a time. For weapon abilities, pick again each time the unit attacks, at the Select Weapons step. For example:\n\n- **[Scouts](vsdata:core-rule/scouts)**: use a distance every model in the unit has (8″ if all have both 6″ and 8″), otherwise the lowest (6″ if 1 model has only 6″ and 5 have 8″).\n- **[[SUSTAINED HITS 1]](vsdata:core-rule/sustained-hits)** and **[[SUSTAINED HITS 2]](vsdata:core-rule/sustained-hits)** are duplicates despite different numbers.\n- **[[ANTI-VEHICLE 4+]](vsdata:core-rule/anti)** and **[[ANTI-INFANTRY 2+]](vsdata:core-rule/anti)** are duplicates despite different keywords.",
